<title>POLAND: ZLOTY FIXED STRONGER AT -0.38 PCT FROM PARITY RATE.</title>
<headline>ZLOTY FIXED STRONGER AT -0.38 PCT FROM PARITY RATE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4730 to the dollar, up from 3.4880 on Friday and at 1.8710 to the mark, up from 1.8735, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.38 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Friday's fix at -0.74 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
